# candidates.tsv.example — copy to candidates.tsv and edit.
#
# SEALED alias->model MAP. Real candidates.tsv is gitignored; do NOT show the
# grader until scores are locked. Aliases are neutral so nothing leaks model id.
#
# TSV columns:
#   alias  platform  model  agent  stage  effort  effort_mechanism
#
# STAGE 1 POLICY (unbiased screen): hold effort CONSTANT at medium across ALL
# cells where the harness lets us set it. Do NOT pin by intended tier — that
# would presuppose the result (a mini that does well at medium would be invisible
# if we forced it to low). Where a harness can't set medium, fall back to its
# default and record that. STAGE 2 sweeps low/medium/high on finalists.
#
# effort: minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh | default
# effort_mechanism (MUST match the harness's real capability — adapters enforce):
#   flag   = Codex   (-c model_reasoning_effort=minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh)
#          = Copilot (--effort / --reasoning-effort = low|medium|high|xhigh; minimal where supported)
#   config = Gemini CLI (writes .gemini/settings.json thinkingLevel; Gemini 3 = minimal|medium|high, NO low)
#   prompt = Claude Code (think/think-hard/ultrathink keyword + maybe --max-thinking-tokens) -> status "approximated"
#          = Cursor (inline natural-language directive in the prompt; UNVERIFIABLE) -> status "requested"
#   none   = a harness with no effort control at all (none currently) -> status "not-applied"
#
# effort_status (derived, kept in sealed metadata; how trustworthy the effort setting is):
#   applied (flag/config) > approximated (claude keywords) > requested (cursor inline) >
#   not-applied > default. Do NOT compare cost across cells of different status as if equal.
#
# GEMINI HAS NO "low": valid thinkingLevel is minimal|medium|high. A Stage-2 Gemini
# sweep therefore uses {minimal, medium, high}. If the effort column says "low" for a
# Gemini cell, the adapter remaps it to "minimal" and flags it.
#
# VERIFY model + effort strings on YOUR installed CLIs before running:
#   copilot --help | codex exec --help | claude --help | cursor-agent --help | gemini --help
# Confirm the exact GPT-5.5 picker name per platform (may be dated / -codex variant).
#
# Auth env: copilot=COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN; codex=`codex login`/CODEX_API_KEY;
#   claude-code=subscription/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; cursor=CURSOR_API_KEY;
#   gemini-cli=GEMINI_API_KEY/GOOGLE_API_KEY.
#
# Phase A ships only the live Stage-1 rows below. Leave Stage-2 examples
# commented out until a later Plan v2 re-opens the extended screen.

# alias   platform    model              agent           stage  effort   effort_mechanism
cand-01	copilot	gpt-5.4-mini	copilot-cli	1	medium	flag
cand-02	copilot	gpt-5.4	copilot-cli	1	medium	flag
cand-03	copilot	claude-opus-4.8	copilot-cli	1	medium	flag
cand-04	claude-code	sonnet	claude-code-cli	1	medium	prompt
cand-05	claude-code	haiku	claude-code-cli	1	medium	prompt
cand-06	cursor	composer-2.5	cursor-cli	1	medium	prompt
cand-17	codex	gpt-5.5	codex-cli	1	medium	flag
cand-18	copilot	gpt-5.5	copilot-cli	1	medium	flag
#
# --- PHASE B / PLAN v2 (commented out intentionally in Phase A) ------------
# cand-07	copilot	gemini-3.5-flash	copilot-cli	2	medium	flag
# cand-08	copilot	gemini-3.1-pro	copilot-cli	2	medium	flag
# cand-09	cursor	gpt-5.4-mini	cursor-cli	2	medium	prompt
# cand-10	cursor	gpt-5.4	cursor-cli	2	medium	prompt
# cand-11	cursor	claude-opus-4.8	cursor-cli	2	medium	prompt
# cand-12	claude-code	opus	claude-code-cli	2	medium	prompt
# cand-13	codex	gpt-5.4-mini	codex-cli	2	medium	flag
# cand-14	codex	gpt-5.4	codex-cli	2	medium	flag
# cand-15	gemini-cli	gemini-3.5-flash	gemini-cli	2	medium	config
# cand-16	gemini-cli	gemini-3.1-pro	gemini-cli	2	medium	config
#
# --- STAGE 2 EFFORT SWEEP (finalists only; example shape) -------------------
# After Stage 1, add low/med/high rows per finalist on a NEW stage tag, e.g.:
# cand-04-lo  claude-code  sonnet  claude-code-cli  2sweep  low     prompt
# cand-04-md  claude-code  sonnet  claude-code-cli  2sweep  medium  prompt
# cand-04-hi  claude-code  sonnet  claude-code-cli  2sweep  high    prompt
# cand-13-lo  codex        gpt-5.4 codex-cli         2sweep  low     flag
# cand-13-md  codex        gpt-5.4 codex-cli         2sweep  medium  flag
# cand-13-hi  codex        gpt-5.4 codex-cli         2sweep  high    flag
# Copilot sweeps cleanly via --effort (status=applied). Cursor sweeps via inline
# directive (status=requested, unverified). Gemini sweeps {minimal,medium,high}.
